'''Mr. Puffington''' (フグ太くん, ''Fuguta-kun'') is a [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemy that appears in [[Legend Stages]]. He was added in [[Version 8.9 Update|Version 8.9]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Mr. Puffington
|image = E 477.png
|money drop = 900¢ - 3,555¢
|first appearance = '''UL''': [[Hot Spring Reception|Sub-chapter 17 - Hot Spring Reception]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Mysterious Captain|Sub-chapter 16 - Mysterious Captain]]
}}

==Enemy==
Mr. Puffington combines some of the qualities found in [[Brollow]] and [[Rain D.]] and deals much higher damage than all other Relic enemies seen at this point in the game. His close-range attack extends up to 350 range and inflicts [[Curse|curse]] for 10 seconds, paralleling the time his attack animation takes to start again.

==Strategy==
Do not use units with low damage per hit because they will constantly knock him back, allowing him to attack more times. This is especially dangerous with his [[Omni Strike]] as he can kill your whole army in one go, and the units that survive are cursed until his attack starts again with '''no''' downtime. Instead, use units with high damage per hit like [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapsticks]]. [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] can also be put to great use, as (when upgraded to level 37) she can survive and 2HKO Mr. Puffington, soloing him completely when alone, or even kill him instantly in [[True Form]]. The debuff from [[:Category:Cats with Slow ability|Cats with Slow abilities]] is great against him, as his standing range is quite low and if he can't get a hit easily, his Omni Strike means nothing. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] is good for this, as he has a massive range advantage over Mr. Puffington. However, do pay attention to the contents of each stage he appears in, as they each feature a different niche and thus must be worked around.

